# Nouns that count people or things a clock never takes: a bare hour behind a
# clock preposition and directly before one of them is a count ("wave at 5
# people").  Each word is quoted from its Wiktionary Noun entry
# (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the fetched pages are kept with the audit.
# Person: Noun. "person, individual"
# Personen: Noun. "plural of Person"
# Leute: Noun. "people several individual persons, a group of people in general, esp. of one kind or another, fol..."
# Gäste: Noun. "form of Gast"
# Nachbarn: Noun. "form of Nachbar"
# Freunde: Noun. "form of Freund"
# Kinder: Noun. "form of Kind"
# Erwachsene: Noun. "female adult"
# Spieler: Noun. "player"
# Plätze: Noun. "form of Platz"
# Tische: Noun. "form of Tisch"
# Karten: Noun. "plural of Karte (cards)"
# Zimmer: Noun. "room separate part of a building, enclosed by walls, a floor and a ceiling"
# Euro: Noun. "euro currency"
person
personen
leute
gäste
nachbarn
freunde
kinder
erwachsene
spieler
plätze
tische
karten
zimmer
euro
